// Copy this file to reconfigure.cmds (gitignored) and edit it to whatever
// sequence of "#..." commands gets the device back to the state you want
// after `make flash` wipes it - see the Makefile's own comment on `flash`
// and `reconfigure`, and scripts/reconfigure.sh for exactly how this file
// gets sent. One command per line; blank lines and "//" comments (like
// these) are skipped, so this file is safe to copy as-is and edit from.

// A fresh registration, consuming a real code and registering under a new
// device_id/secret each time:
#reg,123456,my-device-name

// Once "#nvs" (or a future direct setter) shows you a device_id/secret from
// an earlier registration and you'd rather reuse it than register again,
// replace the "#reg" above with whatever restores that state directly.

// Always useful to see the result:
#stat
